### VS Code ###
.vscode/

### Secrets and key material — never in git ###
# A private key committed once stays in history for ever; removing the file in
# a later commit does not remove it from the earlier one. Keep them out.
*.pem
*.p12
*.jks
*.keystore
src/main/resources/keys/
.env
.env.*
# The template carries no real values and has to be committed -- the setup
# instructions start with `cp .env.example .env`, so an ignored template means
# the first command in the README fails.
!.env.example

### Editor backups and stray archives ###
# Files like `application.properties~` and a hand-made `cryptography.zip` were
# committed by accident. They are build-irrelevant and one of them shipped a
# copy of the configuration, credentials included.
*~
*.zip
*.orig
*.rej
